From 5faf37a6f962a9f9ad62678d1463d77f282978b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:06:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Send the customer receipt and an owner payment notice on
 every successful payment

Automatic receipts never arrived. Three separate causes, all fixed here:

1. A missing receiptSentAt column stopped the receipt entirely. The marker is a
   manual SQL step (0224), so on an un-migrated database claimOrderReceipt
   returned schema_missing and deliverOrderReceipt returned without sending.
   Nobody was emailed. An absent column now sends without deduplication.

2. The Stripe webhook had no invoice.paid handler, so an invoice-paid order was
   never confirmed and never receipted.

3. Email failures sat inside the webhook's try block. sendPaidOrderReceipt
   rethrows when delivery fails, so an email problem became a 500 that made
   Stripe retry a payment that had already succeeded. The email work now lives
   in deliverPaymentEmails, which logs and swallows.

The receipt also no longer invents sales@cabinetdealz.com as a BCC. For an
owner-placed order that address duplicated the recipient and the copy was
dropped, which is why the owner saw nothing. An unset copy address now simply
means no copy.

The owner notice is a new, independent message (paymentNoticeEmail.ts) with its
own claim marker: amount, customer, paid-at, and the Stripe reference. It fires
from checkout completion, payment intent success, invoice.paid, the
Authorize.net card charge, and an admin mark-paid, so a payment recorded any way
produces one notice to ORDER_NOTIFY_EMAIL (falling back to OWNER_EMAIL).

docs/sql/0250 adds paymentNoticeSentAt as one statement for the owner to run.
The notice still sends when that column is absent, so a missing migration can
never silence it again.

Co-authored-by: 7809tom-sys <7809tom-sys@users.noreply.github.com>
